# David 2026-10-17: Hostinger/LiteSpeed's default static-asset caching sends
# "Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800" (7 days) for .js/.css under
# /dev/assets/ -- the SHARED bundle every /props/<slug> property page loads.
# Every property's published HTML bakes in a FROZEN ?v=... query string at
# publish time and never updates it on later deploys (see deploy_dev.py's
# own closing note), so once any browser (David's own test browser
# included) has loaded a given property's exact script URL once, it will
# keep serving that now-stale cached JS for up to 7 days -- completely
# independent of Cloudflare purges and regardless of how many times
# deploy_dev.py uploads fresh code to the server. This is the real root
# cause behind the repeated "I deployed the fix and it's still not working"
# reports today (amenities, dropdown text, image gallery). Fix: force every
# load of these two files to revalidate with the server (a cheap 304 when
# unchanged, the real fresh file when it's not) instead of trusting a
# week-old local cache.
<IfModule mod_headers.c>
  <FilesMatch "\.(js|css)$">
    Header set Cache-Control "no-cache, must-revalidate"
  </FilesMatch>
</IfModule>
<IfModule mod_expires.c>
  <FilesMatch "\.(js|css)$">
    ExpiresActive On
    ExpiresDefault "access"
  </FilesMatch>
</IfModule>
